                <pb facs="0325" n="205" sameAs="frus:frus1931v02/pg205"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/34: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Werlich</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >San José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-12-22T17:00:00-06:00">December 22, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7:56 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>61. Referring to Department’s telegram No. 42, December 20, 1 p.m. The Minister
                    for Foreign Affairs has notified me informally that the <pb facs="0326" n="206"
                        xml:id="pg206"/> Costa Rican Minister at San Salvador will be instructed
                    tomorrow that Costa Rica has decided not to recognize present regime in
                    Salvador.</p>
                <p>Above text telegraphed to Legation at San Salvador December 20, 3 p.m.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Werlich</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
